text = "Lost among the twisting woods, Alice stumbled onward. Brambles tore at her dress, thorns tugged her hair, and every turn led only deeper into the maze of whispering trees. The moonlight fractured between the branches, silver paths leading everywhere—and nowhere.
At last she burst into a clearing where the smell of tea and sugared cakes lingered in the air. There sat the Mad Hatter, grinning wide, his teacup poised in mid-toast as if he had been waiting all along.
“Oh, my dear,” he said, peering at her with eyes alight with mischief and madness, “you’ve come quite undone, haven’t you? Why… you’re even madder than I!”
And with a laugh that rang like broken china, the Hatter set his battered crown upon Alice’s head.
From that night on, the tea party never ended. Alice poured, and Alice laughed, and Alice sang nonsense songs, host to an eternal banquet under an endless sky. Guests came and went, but the table was always full—always waiting—always mad.
In Wonderland, a new Hatter had been crowned.
"
autowrap_mode = 3

